---
import Icon from '~/components/Icon.astro';
import { firms, appLinks } from '~/lib/marketing';
---

<section id="firm-mode" class="py-12 md:py-16 lg:py-20">
  <div class="container-app grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.95fr_1.05fr] lg:items-start">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow"><Icon name="shield" size={14} /> Firm Mode</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4">Prop-firm tracking is included, but it is not the whole pitch.</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-fluid-lg text-muted">
        This is the strongest differentiator because almost nobody treats prop-firm-aware tracking as a first-class product surface. But the page should still lead with the wider Run / Test / Track loop.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-fluid-base text-subtle">
        When you do need it, Firm Mode adds breach gauges, payout countdowns, and rule-aware pre-flight context for the five challenge environments below.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/prop-firms" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-fluid-sm text-brand hover:text-electric">See Firm Mode detail <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={14} /></a>
        <a href={appLinks.signup} class="btn btn-primary" data-cta="firm-mode-start-free">
          Pre-flight in the app
          <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={16} />
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 reveal">
      {firms.map((firm) => (
        <article class="card p-5">
          <h3 class="text-fluid-xl">{firm.name}</h3>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fluid-sm text-muted">
            {firm.rules.map((rule) => (
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="mt-[5px] size-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand"></span><span>{rule}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4 text-fluid-xs text-subtle">{firm.note}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
